I push the cart in the shop.
I like coffee very much.
So I want coffee now.
I look around.
But I do not see coffee here.
The shelves here are very tall.
I see a worker.
I go near him.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, namaste."
"I want coffee."
"But I do not see the right shelf."
"Where are the hot drinks?"
He points to another aisle.
He says, "Madam, they are there."
I say thank you.
I go to that aisle.
Finally, I get the coffee.
